`,t.jsxs(e.p,{children:["When ",t.jsx(e.strong,{children:"Edge"}),' arrived - first the EdgeHTML version, later the Chromium-based one - it felt like the industry exhaling. Not instantly, and not perfectly, but suddenly "test in IE" was no longer the last gate before every release. I do not miss polyfilling ',t.jsx(e.span,{"data-rehype-pretty-code-figure":"",children:t.jsx(e.code,{"data-language":"plaintext","data-theme":"github-dark",children:t.jsx(e.span,{"data-line":"",children:t.jsx(e.span,{children:"Object.assign"})})})})," for a browser that treated the web like a suggestion."]}),`
